, "content": "Belize River Challenge"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le09ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Present vs. The Present Continuous"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Present tense to talk about a routine or a specific action that happens regularly.<br> You can use expressions of frequency like <span class=\"italic\"> every day</span> or <span class=\"italic\">always</span> with the Simple Present.<br><br>You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about an action happening right now. You can also use the Present Continuous to talk about events that  <span class=\"strong\">are happening</span> soon.  You make the Present Continuous with the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be + -ing</span>."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Simple\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I stay in the office until late every day.<br> The race celebrates the Maya culture.<br> I always bring my lunch to work.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm staying in the office until late today.<br> I'm celebrating my friend's birthday later.<br> I'm bringing the tour group on the challenge tomorrow!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Do you usually take part in take part in the River Challenge?<br> When does the race start? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Are you taking part in the River Challenge this year?<br> When is the race starting this week? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I don't usually go sightseeing.<br> He doesn't find museums interesting. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I'm not going sightseeing with the group today.<br> We aren't finding this museum interesting. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to mark"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to remember; to celebrate"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This year marks the 16th anniversary of the race."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about an important event."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "challenge "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something difficult"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Belize River Challenge takes four days to complete."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "annual"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that happens every year "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm participating in the annual Belize River Challenge!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "remarkable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "worthy of admiring"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Mayan culture is remarkable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "legacy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something received from past generations "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The River Challenge celebrates the Mayan legacy in Belize."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "descendant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "from the same family line or culture"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many descendants of the Maya still use the river today."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "I'm having the time of my life!"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "I'm having a lot of fun!"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Belize River Challenge is exciting. I'm having the time of my life!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of an event that happens in your country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a paragraph of 5-8 lines about the event. Include answers to the following questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Why is it special? What does it celebrate?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "How often does it happen? How long does it last?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Who can participate in the event?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the paragraph aloud to your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I compile background information about a national event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about traditions and customs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my paragraph with my partner."}]}], "type": "sena"}